/* book: lead: Every CMOS layer starts as a pattern in a polymer film called resist. Lithography prints that pattern: clean, coat, bake, align a mask, expose, develop. The resist then protects some areas while the layer below is cut away by etching or built up by deposition. Strip the resist and the wafer is ready for the next mask. The same loop runs for every layer, so its resolution sets the smallest transist */
