/* book Worked example: Q: A projection printer uses λ = 248 nm, NA = 0.5 and process factor k = 0.6. (a) Find the smallest printable feature R = k·λ/NA. (b) Find depth of focus DOF = λ/(2NA²). (c) Repeat both for NA = 0.6 and compare.
   1. For NA = 0.5, R = 0.6 × 248 nm / 0.5 = 297.6 nm, about 0.30 μm.
   2. DOF = 248 nm / (2 × 0.5²) = 248 / 0.5 = 496 nm, about 0.50 μm.
   3. For NA = 0.6, R = 0.6 × 248 / 0.6 = 248 nm.
   4. DOF = 248 / (2 × 0.6²) = 248 / 0.72 = 344.4 nm, about 344 nm.
   5. Higher NA improves resolution (R falls from 297.6 nm to 248 nm) but reduces depth of focus (496 nm to 344 nm).
   Answer:  */
