/* book exam traps: Wet etching undercuts the mask: the hole is wider than the window at the surface. A square vertical profile is wrong for wet etch. | Positive resist: the exposed part dissolves. Negative resist: the exposed part stays. Swapping them reverses the whole pattern. | A mask is 1×; a reticle is usually 4× or 5× and the projection lens reduces it. Do not use reticle dimensions directly as wafer dimensions. | R = λ/NA is incomplete; the process factor k (from about 0.8 down to 0.25) must be included. DOF is in nm, not μm, unless converted. | Over-etch is intentional, not a defect; endpoint detection is a signal, not a fixed time. */
